[[Troll]]s can be assigned as a [[Slayer task]] at 60 [[combat level]] by various [[Slayer master]]s. Trolls are, for the most part, found in the [[Fremennik Province]] and north of [[Burthorpe]].

Trolls fought in [[quests]] all count towards the Slayer task, with the exception of sea trolls. The [[boss]]es can be fought again in the [[Nightmare Zone]].

Players who have completed the [[Morytania Diary#Hard|hard Morytania Diary]] might want to bring the [[bonecrusher]] to gain passive [[Prayer]] experience from the [[big bones]] drops. Players with 92 [[Magic]] and the [[Arceuus spellbook]] may opt to use the [[Sinister Offering]] spell instead.

[[File:Slayer Task - Death Plateau Cannon Spot.png|thumb|The neutral tile marker one tile north indicates a possible cannon placement for thrower trolls.]]

There are two types of trolls that players can fight for a troll task: mountain trolls and ice trolls.

[[Mountain troll]]s are found in many locations, primarily around the Fremennik Province, though a group of fourteen trolls are also found in [[Mount Quidamortem]]. The Mount Quidamortem trolls can be easily accessed with the [[Xeric's talisman]] if players have received an [[ancient tablet]] from the [[Chambers of Xeric]] unlocking the Xeric's Honour teleport, although using the [[Lovakengj Minecart Network]] teleport or nearby [[fairy ring]] are also suitable. 

Other variants include [[Thrower Troll|thrower troll]]s and [[troll general]]s, however these are scarce, far, and have nonexistent drops.

The other trolls, [[ice troll]]s, can be found in the [[Ice Path]], [[Trollweiss Dungeon]], and the isles north of [[Neitiznot]] and [[Jatizso]]. 

The trolls in the Ice Path are not worth killing, as these are far stronger than other trolls and have incredibly poor drops for their level. Instead, players are advised to kill the trolls on the isles, as they are weaker, have a slightly better drop table, and are found in larger quantities in an open [[multicombat area]]. If killing trolls here, prayer and a [[Neitiznot shield]] are required in order to reduce damage taken from the [[ice troll female]]s, who are much more accurate and damaging if not using a Neitiznot shield. Out of the two isles, it may be preferable to kill the trolls north of Jatizso, as the trolls there will often focus on the guards fighting them, which will lower the damage the player receives. Additionally, [[Magnus Gram|the bank]] on Jatizso is slightly closer to the troll area than it is on Neitiznot.

Regardless of the troll being killed, a [[dwarf multicannon]] is highly recommended as trolls have low aggression range.

One quick way to complete a trolls task for players not using a dwarf multicannon is to kill the [[ice troll runts]] in the first island north of [[Neitiznot]]. This method requires completion of [[The Fremennik Trials]] to access Neitiznot. There are several guards nearby constantly fighting the trolls, who deal considerable damage and will help speed up kills. They also keep the trolls distracted so that players are able to range or mage without utilising safespots. Note that if guards deal the finishing blow, the Slayer experience received is halved, but drops are still received as long as the player dealt any damage. Fire spells are recommended, as ice trolls have a fire weakness of 100%.

==Recommendations==
*Medium [[combat]] stats. See the skill levels below for an indication of the advised stats:
*Level {{SCP|Attack|40}} or higher.
*Level {{SCP|Strength|40}} or higher.
*Level {{SCP|Prayer|43}} or higher for [[Protect from Melee]] strongly recommended
*Completion of {{SCP|Quest}} [[The Fremennik Trials]] to be able to speak to [[Mord Gunnars]] for access to [[Jatizso]] for [[ice trolls]].
**{{SCP|Quest}} [[The Fremennik Isles]] does not need to be completed to access [[Jatizso]] as Mord takes the player at the start of the quest.
*Completion of {{SCP|Quest}} [[Dwarf Cannon]] to be able to use a [[dwarf multicannon]].

